      "title": "Quad foreign ministers express grave concern over economic coercion",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/quad-foreign-ministers-express-grave-concern-over-economic-coercion-126110100009_1.html",
      "description": "The Quad foreign ministers on Saturday expressed \"grave concern\" over \"economic coercion\" through arbitrary export restrictions and practices that disrupt global supply chains.\nIn an apparent reference to China, the foreign ministers of India, the US, Australia and Japan expressed grave concerns regarding economic coercion, including arbitrary export restrictions, as well as non-market policies and practices that result in overcapacity, disrupting global supply chains in critical industries.\nIn a joint statement after their meeting in Atlanta, the Quad foreign ministers reiterated their commitment to building reliable and open global supply chains and trusted and resilient infrastructure.\nThe Quad Foreign Ministers' Meeting was convened by US Secretary of State Marco Rubio and was attended by External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar, Australian Foreign Minister Penny Wong and Japanese Foreign Minister Toshimitsu Motegi.\nThe ministers recognised the importance of critical sea lanes, t",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-01T02:13:47"
    },
    {
      "title": "Secure supply chains, resilience key for global economy: Jaishankar at G20",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/secure-supply-chains-resilience-key-for-global-economy-jaishankar-at-g20-126110100012_1.html",
      "description": "External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar on Saturday said securing supply chains and ensuring their resilience was central to the well-being of the global economy.\nAddressing the concluding plenary of the G20 Foreign Ministers' Meeting in Atlanta, Jaishankar said diversification and de-risking, including in connectivity, are key to supply chain resilience, threatened by pandemics, conflicts, climate events and mishaps.\n\"The right to industrialise must be promoted; predatory practices and targeting competition should be firmly resisted,\" the minister said in a post on X, sharing the broad issues he raised at the G20 meeting convened by US Secretary of State Marco Rubio.\nThe minister said de-concentration of the global economy and optimisation of production across geographies can discourage the weaponisation of finance, resources, production and market share.\n\"The G20 should work towards de-politicisation of markets,\" Jaishankar said.\nThe minister said G20 countries must reconcile the",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-01T02:07:28"
    },
    {
      "title": "Jaishankar calls for deeper Quad cooperation on energy, maritime security",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/jaishankar-calls-for-deeper-quad-cooperation-on-energy-maritime-security-126103101400_1.html",
      "description": "External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar on Saturday stressed the importance of deepening cooperation among Quad nations to promote supply chain resilience and ensure technology, critical minerals, and energy security.\nParticipating in the Quad Foreign Ministers' Meeting in Atlanta, Jaishankar said he spoke about countering non-market practices and increased economic stresses in the Indo-Pacific region.\nThe Quad Foreign Ministers' Meeting was held on the sidelines of the G20 Foreign Ministers' Meeting in Atlanta on Saturday, convened by US Secretary of State Marco Rubio. Foreign Ministers of Australia and Japan -- Penny Wong and Toshimitsu Motegi, respectively -- also attended the meeting.\nJaishankar said he highlighted the importance of maintaining stability, driving prosperity and ensuring freedom of choice as continuing commitments in the Indo-Pacific.\nThe minister also underscored taking forward agreements on counter-terrorism, maritime security and capacity building to enhance .",
